--- Mrs. Ada Turner's diary, Friday, the 14th of March, 1930 (4/4 key facts kept) ---
I found a half-crown under Mr. Hale's desk, and kept it. Bert and I spoke together about the work at the docks, and he gave me 3s. 6d., half the week's rent.
   ◇ Arthur reflects: Mr. Thomas appears to be an honest, straight-forward man of business.
   ◇ Arthur reflects: He thinks Mrs. Turner a dishonest person.

--- Mr. Arthur Hale's diary, Friday, the 14th of March, 1930 (2/3 key facts kept) ---
I searched for the half-crown, but could not find it. I spoke to Mr. Thomas about our work, and he paid me my week's wages. I spoke to him also about the news in the paper, and he gave me 40 shillings for household expenses.
   ◇ Mr. Thomas reflects: He thinks Mr. Arthur Hale a steady and respectable young man.

--- Mr. Walter Thomas's diary, Friday, the 14th of March, 1930 (1/1 key facts kept) ---
I spoke with Mr. Hale about the ledger, and learned that he had got through half of it. I spoke to him about the news, and he told me of the death of the Emperor of China.

